blocks.en:
Our contributions are threefold:(1) Process-aware evaluation of agent capability. We formulate agent evaluation around the distinction between realized outcomes and the mechanisms that produce them, combining task performance, controlled mechanism effects, and trace-derived diagnostics;
(2) Controlled diagnosis of agentic mechanisms. LiveMACEBench evaluates Tool Use , Persistent Memory , Rule Following , and Multi-Agent Collaboration under matched backbones, environments, and interaction protocols, enabling capability differences and failure modes to be localized rather than inferred from aggregate performance.
(3) A naturally evolving testbed for persistent evaluation. We instantiate this framework in live financial markets, where external conditions evolve continuously and agent actions have persistent consequences, enabling capability evaluation along open-ended trajectories.

blocks.zh:
我们的贡献有三个:(1) 对代理能力进行过程认识评价。 我们围绕已实现的成果与产生成果的机制之间的区别制定代理人评价,将任务绩效、控制机制效应和微量衍生诊断结合起来;
(2)受控地诊断出剂机制. LiveMACEBench在匹配的主干、环境和互动协议下评价工具使用、持续记忆、规则跟踪和多代理协作,使能力差异和失败模式能够本地化,而不是从聚合性能中推断出来。
(3) 持续评价的自然演进试验床。 我们在活跃的金融市场中迅速利用这一框架,在金融市场中,外部条件不断演变,代理人行动产生持续的后果,使能力评估能够沿着无限制的轨道进行。

